te-v-jeffries/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Jeffries\">105 Wash. 2d 398</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9850373\"><a href=\"/opinion/1279670/state-v-jeffries/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Jeffries\">717 P. 2d 722</a></span>; No. 86-5381, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1499723\"><a href=\"/opinion/1499723/hogue-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Hogue v. State\">711 S. W. 2d 9</a></span>; No. 86-5452, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9641548\"><a href=\"/opinion/1499743/state-v-driscoll/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Driscoll\">711 S. W. 2d 512</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9058476,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":597,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b860-14\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"AYrt\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b860-15\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual'punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}